From: sjcsf <346224915+llsf2020@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:05:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] FreeChat: metadata minimization; expiry markers and
 immediate purge

- Devices: never store IP addresses or device names (also on rename);
  last-seen rounded down to the day
- Messages under a room TTL or a sender's burn-after-read carry
  unsigned.com.freechat.expires_at / com.freechat.read_ttl, so clients
  delete their local copy on their own
- On expiry the server purges the event outright (no redaction, no
  skeleton) via a new timeline purge_pdu, and deletes its media; when the
  purged event was a forward extremity the room's extremities move back
  to the newest remaining event so the room keeps working
